    <!-- Shown in the settings guide card while each layout is focused; same order as the values -->
    <string-array name="library_layout_summaries">
        <item>One centred carousel: the focused cover sits big in the middle with its title and Play underneath, and the other games shrink towards the edges.</item>
        <item>Every cover at once in a grid, with nothing else on screen. Selecting a game opens its page, with Play and its options.</item>
        <item>The focused game\'s cover fills the left side of the screen, with its title and Play beside it and a strip of the other covers along the bottom.</item>
        <item>Game names in large type with a big cover beside them. The easiest to read from the couch; A plays the highlighted game.</item>
    </string-array>
    <!-- Shown in the settings guide card while each mode is focused; same order as the values -->
    <string-array name="video_frame_pacing_summaries">
        <item>Prefer lowest latency plus LFR: the decoder is checked more often and only the newest frame is ever shown. The most responsive mode; can skip a frame now and then.</item>
        <item>Asks the PC for 4× your frame rate and shows only the newest frame. Only cuts delay if the game really renders that fast; raise the bitrate to keep quality.</item>
        <item>Asks the PC for 2× your frame rate and shows only the newest frame. Only cuts delay if the game really renders that fast; raise the bitrate to keep quality.</item>
        <item>Shows each frame as soon as it\'s decoded and drops ones that arrive late. The least delay; motion can look a little uneven when the network wobbles.</item>
        <item>Shows frames in step with the TV\'s refresh, keeping one in reserve to smooth over hiccups. Smooth motion for a little more delay.</item>
        <item>Asks the PC for one frame per second less than the TV\'s refresh (59 at 60 Hz) so frames never pile up. Smooth with little delay; one repeated frame each second.</item>
        <item>Never drops a frame, even when they back up. The smoothest motion, but delay can build up noticeably; best for slow-paced games.</item>
    </string-array>

